A DMA channel may be bound twice.
The channel table would name the second Dma alone, and the first would run a channel it no longer has;
at most one Dma is bound to any channel.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: dma is missing from the channel table
Witness: fuzz dma-bind-checks

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -894,9 +894,7 @@ static int op_dma_line(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         if (pool->dying) {
             return KERR_STATE;
         }
-        if (dma_binding(channel) != NULL) {
-            return KERR_OVERLAP;
-        }
+
         /* The invoked slot is cleared below, so it may receive the Dma capability, under whichever number names it. */
         if (slot_at(t, arg[2]) != slot_node(t, slot)) {
             err = slot_vacant(t, arg[2]);
